<title>GREECE: Greek inflation slows to 5.4 pct yr/yr in July.</title>
<headline>Greek inflation slows to 5.4 pct yr/yr in July.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek consumer price inflation slipped to 5.4 percent year-on-year in July from 5.5 percent in June, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said.</p>
<p>The drop was in line with market expectations for July.  </p>
<p>The CPI dropped 1.9 percent month-on-month, NSS said.</p>
<p>    Consumer Price Index     July 97   June 97   July 96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month	     -1.9%	0.4%     -1.7%</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		  5.4%	5.5%	8.2%</p>
<p>    Index (1994=100)	  123.1     125.0     116.8</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
